  "text_input": "Patient presented with generalized weakness and fatigue for 1 month, associated with decreased appetite. He also complained of increased frequency of micturition for 3 months. History of iron transfusion twice. Not a known case of T2DM or HTN. Physical examination revealed pallor. Investigations showed Hemoglobin 9.1 g/dL, WBC 5860 cells/\u00b5L, Platelets 3.73 lakhs/\u00b5L, Urea 23 mg/dL, and Creatinine 0.8 mg/dL. USG abdomen showed renal cysts and a prostate volume of 16-18cc. 2D Echo revealed an EF of 58% with LV diastolic dysfunction. Endoscopy confirmed antral gastritis. The patient was diagnosed with Iron Deficiency Anemia, Antral Gastritis, and Bladder Outlet Obstruction. Treatment included Inj FCM (Iron), Inj Meconerve, and Cap Silodol M.",
